        desc: "France's oldest brandy appellation, produced in the Gascony region (Gers department). Three sub-zones: Bas-Armagnac (finest, sandy soils — 'Sandy Armagnac'), Ténarèze (central, mix of clay and chalk), and Haut-Armagnac (eastern, chalky). Armagnac uses the distinctive continuous Armagnac still (alembic armagnacais), distilling to a lower strength (~52-60% abv) than Cognac, retaining more congeners and producing a more rustic, complex character.",
